<title>USA: Porsche 4-month sales up 25.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Porsche 4-month sales up 25.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German sportscar maker Dr Ing.h.c.F Porsche AG said on Tuesday that sales during the first four months of the 1996/97 business year climbed 25.7 percent to 1.13 billion marks.</p>
<p>Deliveries over the period climbed 29.7 percent to 8,343 units while production climbed 39 percent to 8,595 units. Porsche's hot-selling new Boxster model accounted for 1,456 units of the production climb.</p>
<p>The company's business year ends on July 31.</p>
</text>
